From 5c79b53d3ae1bf1f8be3ec4d094932f68a314d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "thang.luu" <thang.luu@titancorpvn.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 09:17:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(indicators): streaming engines for O(window) live ticks

IndicatorController.onBar recalculated every active indicator over the
full bar history on each tick - O(history) per indicator per tick. On
50k bars with 5 active indicators that measures ~39ms per tick (a
frozen UI at 30 ticks/s) plus a full O(history) IndicatorBar re-map
allocation per tick.

This change:

- Adds an optional `streaming(inputs)` factory to IndicatorDef
  returning a StreamingIndicator: `next(bar)` commits a confirmed bar,
  `peek(bar)` previews the in-progress bar without mutating state.
  onBar uses it when present (in-progress bar is previewed via peek,
  committed exactly once via next on rollover); defs without one keep
  the batch fallback. Measured ~39ms -> ~1ms per tick.
- Ships self-contained streaming engines for all 9 builtins (original
  MIT code, no third-party runtime), verified value-identical to their
  batch `calculate` by a bar-for-bar parity test suite.
- Caches the IndicatorBar conversion and updates it incrementally on
  ticks instead of re-mapping the whole history.
- Fixes RSI warmup to TradingView semantics: the first change is
  bar0->bar1 (ta.change is na on bar 0) instead of a synthetic zero
  change at bar 0, so the first defined RSI lands on bar index
  `length` with an unskewed Wilder seed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
